# STANDING three-way comparison config (CLAUDE.md; METHODOLOGY "Comparison dataset - nomag"); first written as a test, loaded on top
# of gnss_denied.parm (last in the --add-param-file chain) for a one-off
# test of whether EKF3 can fly with no yaw source at all, matching the
# UKF/FGO's actual sensor set. See CLAUDE.md / UKF design report for the
# audit that found EKF3 fusing the compass (EK3_SRC1_YAW=1) despite
# gnss_denied.parm never mentioning it - outside the thesis's stated
# IMU+flow+LiDAR sensor suite.
#
# Parameter set follows ArduPilot's own documented "no yaw sensor" playbook
# (EK3_MAG_CAL's @Description, AP_NavEKF3.cpp): disable the compass fully
# (not just as an EKF3 source - COMPASS_ENABLE/COMPASS_USE* are a separate
# path from EK3_SRC1_YAW, confirmed via AP_Arming_Copter.cpp's
# compass_checks()/arm_checks() and NavEKF3_core::using_noncompass_for_yaw()),
# and set the GSF run/use masks to match EK3_IMU_MASK (both already default
# to 3, matching EK3_IMU_MASK's default of 3 - set explicitly here for
# self-documentation, not because a value needs to change).
#
# NOTE: GSF is a documented fallback in ArduPilot's own playbook, but is
# unconditionally unavailable in THIS config - runYawEstimatorPrediction()/
# Correction() (AP_NavEKF3_Control.cpp) gate on EK3_SRC1_POSXY/VELXY being
# GPS, which gnss_denied.parm already sets to None/OpticalFlow. So this
# config genuinely has zero yaw reference, not GSF-backed - that's the
# point of the test.
#
# REVISION after first test attempt failed to arm ("Compass 1 not healthy"):
# COMPASS_ENABLE=0 was wrong. AP_Arming_Copter::arm_checks() has its OWN
# compass-health gate (AP_Arming_Copter.cpp:575, #ifndef ALLOW_ARM_NO_COMPASS,
# not defined for this SITL build), separate from the generic
# AP_Arming::compass_checks(). It only skips if ahrs.using_noncompass_for_yaw()
# is true; tracing that (NavEKF3_core::using_noncompass_for_yaw(),
# AP_NavEKF3_Control.cpp:642) shows it requires a *recent* (<5s) non-compass
# yaw fusion event (GPS/GSF/extnav) - none of which can ever happen in this
# no-GPS config - so it always calls _compass.healthy(), which needs the
# compass driver to actually exist and report healthy, i.e. COMPASS_ENABLE=1.
# This check is unconditional - not gated behind check_enabled()/ARMING_SKIPCHK
# (ARMING_CHECK before the 4.7 rename), and runs before should_skip_all_checks() - so no ARMING_SKIPCHK bitmask
# exclusion can bypass it either; COMPASS_ENABLE=1 is the only source-backed
# option. EKF3 still gets zero yaw information from it: EK3_SRC1_YAW=0 means
# setYawSource() never selects COMPASS regardless of driver health, and
# COMPASS_USE*=0 independently keeps it out of the generic compass_checks()
# and AP_Compass::use_for_yaw(). The compass stays "present and healthy" only
# to satisfy this one arming-safety gate; it contributes nothing to the state
# estimate - verified in Step 3 below (XKFS.MAG_FUSION, XKF3.IYAW, XKF2 mag
# states, MAG message count).
EK3_SRC1_YAW 0
COMPASS_ENABLE 1
COMPASS_USE 0
COMPASS_USE2 0
COMPASS_USE3 0
EK3_GSF_RUN_MASK 3
EK3_GSF_USE_MASK 3
